    "1/1": "Let's break down the bug and generate the required patches:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Bug Scenario Image Analysis & Root Cause Reasoning\n\n**Bug Scenario Image Description:**\n- The DAP (Dynamic Assessment Plugin) accessibility checker reports: \"Each form control must have associated label\".\n- The error is triggered for skeleton components of Accordion and Button in Carbon React.\n- The HTML shows `<button type=\"button\" class=\"bx--accordion__heading\">` and similar elements without any accessible label (no `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, or visible text).\n\n**Root Cause:**\n- Skeleton components are meant to show loading placeholders, but interactive elements like `<button>` and `<a role=\"button\">` are rendered without any accessible label or description.\n- This violates accessibility rules, as all interactive elements must have an accessible name, even in skeleton/loading states.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Bug Code Snippet Analysis & Bug Location\n\n#### **A. Accordion Skeleton**\n- File: `packages/react/src/components/Accordion/Accordion.Skeleton.js`\n- Problem: The `<button>` in both `AccordionSkeleton` and `AccordionSkeletonItem` has no accessible label.\n\n#### **B. Button Skeleton**\n- File: `packages/react/src/components/Button/Button.Skeleton.js`\n- Problem: The `<div>` (for button) and `<a role=\"button\">` (for anchor) have no accessible label.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Generate Patches\n\n#### **A. Accordion Skeleton Patch**\n\nAdd `aria-label=\"Loading accordion section\"` to the `<button>` elements in both `AccordionSkeleton` and `AccordionSkeletonItem`.\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/Accordion/Accordion.Skeleton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n          <button type=\"button\" className={`${prefix}--accordion__heading`}>\n            <ChevronRight16 className={`${prefix}--accordion__arrow`} />\n            <SkeletonText className={`${prefix}--accordion__title`} />\n          </button>\n=======\n          <button\n            type=\"button\"\n            className={`${prefix}--accordion__heading`}\n            aria-label=\"Loading accordion section\"\n            tabIndex={-1}\n            disabled\n          >\n            <ChevronRight16 className={`${prefix}--accordion__arrow`} />\n            <SkeletonText className={`${prefix}--accordion__title`} />\n          </button>\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/Accordion/Accordion.Skeleton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n    <li className={`${prefix}--accordion__item`}>\n      <button type=\"button\" className={`${prefix}--accordion__heading`}>\n        <ChevronRight16 className={`${prefix}--accordion__arrow`} />\n        <SkeletonText className={`${prefix}--accordion__title`} />\n      </button>\n    </li>\n=======\n    <li className={`${prefix}--accordion__item`}>\n      <button\n        type=\"button\"\n        className={`${prefix}--accordion__heading`}\n        aria-label=\"Loading accordion section\"\n        tabIndex={-1}\n        disabled\n      >\n        <ChevronRight16 className={`${prefix}--accordion__arrow`} />\n        <SkeletonText className={`${prefix}--accordion__title`} />\n      </button>\n    </li>\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n#### **B. Button Skeleton Patch**\n\nAdd `aria-label=\"Loading button\"` to both the `<div>` and `<a>` elements, and set `tabIndex={-1}` and `aria-disabled=\"true\"` to ensure they are not focusable or interactive in skeleton state.\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/Button/Button.Skeleton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n  const button = <div {...commonProps} />;\n=======\n  const button = (\n    <div\n      {...commonProps}\n      aria-label=\"Loading button\"\n      tabIndex={-1}\n      aria-disabled=\"true\"\n    />\n  );\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n```javascript\n### packages/react/src/components/Button/Button.Skeleton.js\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n  const anchor = <a {...commonProps} href={href} role=\"button\" />; // eslint-disable-line\n=======\n  const anchor = (\n    <a\n      {...commonProps}\n      href={href}\n      role=\"button\"\n      aria-label=\"Loading button\"\n      tabIndex={-1}\n      aria-disabled=\"true\"\n    />\n  ); // eslint-disable-line\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Accordion Skeleton:** Add `aria-label`, `tabIndex={-1}`, and `disabled` to all skeleton `<button>`s.\n- **Button Skeleton:** Add `aria-label`, `tabIndex={-1}`, and `aria-disabled=\"true\"` to all skeleton `<div>` and `<a>` elements.\n\nThese changes ensure that all interactive elements in skeleton states are accessible and do not trigger DAP accessibility violations."
